A||||12||My7Fieros||Fuel pump accessable W/O dropping tank?||||2||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||06-19-2001||06:41 PM||||While on vacation in Orange Beach Al/Perdido Bay, Fl a couple of weeks ago, I was at a restaurant talking to this guy that pulled up in an 86 Gt. We were talking (obviously) about Fieros, and he told me he pulled out his console and there was a "hatch" of sorts that led to the fuel pump in the gas tank. He said it made changing the pump much easier.<BR>I didnt acknowledge him about that, because in all my dealings w/ Fieros, Ive never heard of this........poss any truth? Just courious. M7F||||reg||2
Z||000001||Greg Piet||06-19-2001||06:44 PM||||NO.<BR>there are long metal tubes coming from the top cap on the tank.<BR>I have cut apart a Fiero frame, and there was no hatch that could allow the removal of the entire tank cap/tubing.<BR>That was an 85 Fiero I dealt with.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Toddster||06-19-2001||06:50 PM||||What Greg said, "NO".<P>But dropping the tank is not too hard. You must have a car hoist though. Don't try to do it with jack stands you'll drive yourself insane.<P>Whatever you do, do not disconnect anymore hoses than you absolutley need to because you will spend hours trying to re-connect them. Swing the tank down from the front (empty preferably) and pull the pump out carefully. You might want to take the time to put a multimeter on the new float to make sure the the "F" is Full and "E" is Empty on you gauge. The float should read 90 ohms full and 0 ohms empty. It has an adjustment screw.<P>Lotsa Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dslice||06-19-2001||07:03 PM||||I did it with jack stands and it was a snap. Four stands on each corner and then I used the jack to hold up and lower the tank when I removed the brackets that hold the tank up.<BR>Took me about twenty minutes, most of that time trying to remove the the rubber hoses from the metal lines, they tend to stick to metal.<P>Rick<BR>86GT<BR>84Coup<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierofrek||06-19-2001||08:26 PM||||I did it with ramps bought a wally world for $18. biggest prob was getting the fill tube back on correctly||||reg||1
Z||000005||EdsB52||06-19-2001||08:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dslice:<BR><B>I did it with jack stands and it was a snap. Four stands on each corner and then I used the jack to hold up and lower the tank when I removed the brackets that hold the tank up.<BR>Took me about twenty minutes, most of that time trying to remove the the rubber hoses from the metal lines, they tend to stick to metal.<P>Rick<BR>86GT<BR>84Coup</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Wow, 4 jack stands on each corner, you must have a heavy Fiero!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">   <P>Just kidin', I agree with you, Just get the thing up as high as is safe. I actually mark and cut the small rubber lines and install new ones going back in, one line at a time. This is easier than trying to remove each line from its respective steel line and then reinstalling it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fyerstarter||06-19-2001||09:52 PM||||Yeah when I did mine my nose was about touching the bottom of the car. It was a pain in the ass! But I didn't have a very tall jack to get it up on the stands :\ Also the car wouldn't run so I had to siphon a full tank of gas out by hand. Not much fun.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GTZ34||06-20-2001||08:29 AM||||Anyone have a guesstimate on how much clearance is needed to pull the tank?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||06-20-2001||09:30 AM||||i've done a couple of 4cyls. and should be doing a 6cyl sometime soon. is there anything that makes it any harder? ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||06-20-2001||10:37 AM||||Clearance? Your body plus 6 to 8 inches. I have done it twice in my Formula. Not too hard. The painful part is just pulling/reconnecting the hoses. Specially if you have big hands.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||My7Fieros||06-20-2001||06:17 PM||||Thanx, thats what I thought...just had to double check. M7F||||reg||1
